OL,3,AKing leads solemn Remembrance Sunday
OL,4,Aservice at Cenotaph
OL,5,
OL,6,FKing Charles III led the nation in a
OL,7,Fsolemn two-minute silence on
OL,8,FRemembrance Sunday in London to honour
OL,9,Fveterans who had died in conflict.
OL,11,FOn a stone-grey autumn morning, he laid
OL,12,Fa wreath at the Cenotaph in Whitehall
OL,13,Fbefore a march-past by 10,000 armed
OL,14,Fforces veterans.
OL,16,FThat included a shrinking number of
OL,17,FWorld War Two veterans, with 12 taking
OL,18,Fpart this year, including 103-year-old
OL,19,FAnnie Duplock, who described it as a
OL,20,F"very emotional day".
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
